1
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:05,284
This is a test suite for a

2
00:00:05,284 --> 00:00:08,558
semantic model, drawn as a circuit board.

3
00:00:09,008 --> 00:00:12,621
Each chip is a measure, and each probe soldered to

4
00:00:12,621 --> 00:00:15,728
it is a test case with the value we expect.

5
00:00:16,742 --> 00:00:19,744
Green probes pass, red fails with the gap

6
00:00:19,744 --> 00:00:23,112
shown, and amber means the query itself broke.

7
00:00:23,562 --> 00:00:27,022
The dark one is a disabled case, so it gets no power.

8
00:00:27,829 --> 00:00:31,819
I run the suite. Current flows from the model connector

9
00:00:31,819 --> 00:00:34,649
to each query in flight, two at a time.

10
00:00:35,099 --> 00:00:37,766
Probes light up as the results stream back,

11
00:00:37,766 --> 00:00:40,309
and the monitor counts them as they land.

12
00:00:41,112 --> 00:00:44,362
Today ranks what needs attention after the run.

13
00:00:44,812 --> 00:00:50,139
The first item flies to the failing probe: sales for

14
00:00:50,139 --> 00:00:55,262
2025 came back at 13,709 against a plan of 15,000.

15
00:00:56,062 --> 00:00:58,492
Lenses repaint the same board.

16
00:00:58,942 --> 00:01:02,961
Duration shows the slowest queries, and flakiness shows

17
00:01:02,961 --> 00:01:06,542
which probes keep flipping between pass and fail.

18
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:12,330
Short circuit explains every error in plain words.

19
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:16,345
Here a measure was renamed, so the model cannot find

20
00:01:16,345 --> 00:01:19,430
Revenue YTD, and the fix sits right under it.

21
00:01:20,236 --> 00:01:23,250
The probe adds a case. I give it a measure and

22
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:26,396
a filter, and it takes a live reading as I type.

23
00:01:26,846 --> 00:01:30,021
One click copies the reading into the expected value,

24
00:01:30,021 --> 00:01:32,716
and the new probe is soldered onto the board.

25
00:01:39,919 --> 00:01:44,261
The oscilloscope traces every probe across runs, so a

26
00:01:44,261 --> 00:01:47,129
flaky test shows up as a busy wave.

27
00:01:47,934 --> 00:01:51,028
View as developer shows what a teammate sees: they can

28
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:53,664
run any suite, but every edit control is gone.

29
00:01:54,505 --> 00:01:58,059
Save the numbers that matter, run them after every model

30
00:01:58,059 --> 00:02:01,105
change, and see what broke before your users do.
